course: dictionary
lesson: 3316
title: Europe, one of the seven continents
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Europe is one of the seven continents of the world. A continent is a very large area of land, and Europe is one of the biggest on our planet. Many countries lie inside it, such as France, Germany, Italy and Spain.
explain: Europe is a proper noun, which is the name of one particular place, so it starts with a capital letter. Look at the sentence «Spices were dear in medieval Europe» to see how it is used. The words around it tell you that Europe is a place where people lived and traded long ago.
explain: Where is Europe on the map? It lies north of Africa and west of Asia. Many different languages are spoken there, which is one reason it is so interesting to study.
fact: Europe is one of the seven continents of the world.
fact: France, Germany, Italy, Spain, Poland, Ireland, the United Kingdom and Ukraine are all in Europe.
fact: Europe lies north of Africa and west of Asia.
fact: «Raccoons» were brought to Europe, and some escaped; now they live wild in Germany.
fact: In history, many people from Europe travelled to America, Australia and New Zealand.
exercise: Which of these is one of the seven continents of the world? | Poland | Ireland | Ukraine | *Europe
exercise: «Raccoons were brought to Europe and some escaped; now they live wild in Germany.» Where do wild raccoons now live? | Spain | Ukraine | *Germany | Italy
exercise: Europe lies north of which continent? | Australia | *Africa | Asia | America
test: Europe lies west of which continent? | Africa | *Asia | Australia | America
test: «The Statue of Liberty was a gift from France.» Which country gave the Statue of Liberty? | Spain | Poland | Italy | *France
exam: Why does Europe start with a capital letter? | Because it is the name of an animal | Because it is at the start of every sentence | *Because it is a proper noun, the name of one particular place | Because it is a long word
